# Frontend

- Vite + React + TypeScript in `frontend/`
- Two layouts: `PublicLayout` (seeker: `/`, `/search`, `/jobs/:id`, `/alerts/new`, and the email link pages `/a/c/:token`, `/a/:token`, `/a/u/:token`) and `OpsLayout` (`/ops/*`)
- Pages: `frontend/src/pages/public/` and `frontend/src/pages/ops/`
- API client in `frontend/src/api/` - types mirror backend DTOs; `useSearch` → `GET /api/search`
- TanStack Query for data fetching; poll scrape overview 5s when active, 30s otherwise
- Dev proxy: `/api` → `http://localhost:50423` in `frontend/vite.config.ts`
- Shared components in `frontend/src/components/`
- Read-only against the API except alert subscription endpoints (`/api/alerts/*`). No auth; alert management uses capability tokens sent in the `X-Alert-Token` header, never in query strings or browser storage
- Alert UI is hidden when `GET /api/alerts/criteria-options` fails (`useAlertsAvailable`), because the backend only registers alert endpoints when `Alerts:Enabled` is true
- `/a/*` pages call `useNoReferrer()` so the token in the path never leaks through a Referer header
- Confirmation tokens are single use: guard the confirm call against StrictMode's double effect
- After changes: `npm run build` is sufficient. Do not start `npm run dev` unless the user asks.
